\subsubsection{Period $N = 52$}
The period $N=52$ is realised by $113$ parameter sets across $2\\times2$, $2\\times3$, $2\\times4$, $2\\times6$, $3\\times3$, $3\\times4$, $3\\times6$, $4\\times4$, $4\\times6$, $6\\times6$. The reflection parameters take values in $\{$0.0650$, $0.3369$, $0.4303$, $0.5353$, $0.7470$, $0.7607$, $0.9427$\}$, and the phase parameters in $\{$0.0000\pi$, $0.5000\pi$, $1.0000\pi$, $1.5000\pi$\}$. This is one of the longest periods in the classification,
and is confined to a small number of tori whose revival
period sets intersect at a large common value.
